{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "prayer-11-january-1834", "page": "5", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_043_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "43", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/1"}, {"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_044_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "44", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/2"}, {"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_045_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "45", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/3"}, {"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_046_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "46", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/4"}, {"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_047_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "47", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/5"}, {"image": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_048_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "48", "href": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/6"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "prayer-11-january-1834", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD3", "documentSeriesTitle": "Prayer, 11 January 1834", "editorialPageNumber": "47", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/53991743/53991743-0005.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> may not be hindered, but that men’s eyes may thereby be opened to see the truth.</div><div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sixthly, That the Lord would deliver <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10335911290130217001\"><a href=\"#10335911290130217001\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, and gather in his scattered people, to possess it in peace;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4319940443918960378\"><a href=\"#4319940443918960378\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In December 1833, <a href=\"/person/william-wines-phelps\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William W. Phelps</a> <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" poptitle=\"Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 December\n1833\">wrote</a> that church members in <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a> were scattered in <a href=\"/place/clay-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Clay</a>, <a href=\"/place/ray-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Ray</a>, <a href=\"/place/lafayette-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lafayette</a>, <a href=\"/place/jackson-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jackson</a>, and Van Buren counties, and that their “situation . . . affords a gloomy prospect.” However, a JS <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> dictated that same month promised that church members in Missouri would again possess their lands in Jackson County: “<a href=\"/topic/zion\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Zion</a> shall not be moved out of her place notwithstanding her children are scattered they that remain and are pure in heart shall return and come to their <a href=\"/topic/inheritance\" class=\"referenceInPop\">inheritances</a>.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" poptitle=\"Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 December\n1833\">Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 Dec. 1833</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:17–18].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> and also, while in their dispersion, that he would provide for them that they perish not with hunger nor cold. And finally, that God in the name of Jesus would gather his elect speedily, and unveil his face that his saints [p. 47]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> may not be hindered, but <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that men’s eyes may thereby <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be opened to see the truth.</div><div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sixthly, That the Lord would <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>deliver <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2507958668671437541\"><a href=\"#2507958668671437541\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, and gather in <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>his scattered people, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to possess it in peace;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5987055958964075092\"><a href=\"#5987055958964075092\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In December 1833, <a href=\"/person/william-wines-phelps\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William W. Phelps</a> <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" poptitle=\"Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 December\n1833\">wrote</a> that church members in <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a> were scattered in <a href=\"/place/clay-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Clay</a>, <a href=\"/place/ray-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Ray</a>, <a href=\"/place/lafayette-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lafayette</a>, <a href=\"/place/jackson-county-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jackson</a>, and Van Buren counties, and that their “situation . . . affords a gloomy prospect.” However, a JS <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> dictated that same month promised that church members in Missouri would again possess their lands in Jackson County: “<a href=\"/topic/zion\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Zion</a> shall not be moved out of her place notwithstanding her children are scattered they that remain and are pure in heart shall return and come to their <a href=\"/topic/inheritance\" class=\"referenceInPop\">inheritances</a>.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-william-w-phelps-15-december-1833\" poptitle=\"Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 December\n1833\">Letter from William W. Phelps, 15 Dec. 1833</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:17–18].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and also, while in their <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>dispersion, that he would <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>provide for them that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>they perish not with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>hunger nor cold. <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>And finally, that God <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in the name of Jesus <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>would gather his elect <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>speedily, and unveil <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>his face that his saints [p. 47]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Prayer, 11 January 1834", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/prayer-11-january-1834/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Journal, 1832–1834", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/journal-1832-1834/44", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-1_047_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/6662/6662_ms155_1_01_jsj-